A simple implementation of a sorted list in Golang.

Allows for 0(n) insertion, removal, and searching.

Examples are available in the main.go file

Node (n):
- n.Next() : Returns the next linked node.
- n.Prev() :  Returns the previous linked node.


List (l):
- New(vals ...cmp.Order)           : Returns new List with vals [constrained by type in cmp.Ordered] added. O(n) Find operations.
        NOTE: - Smallest Memory footprint.
              - O(n) Find operations.
              - O(n) Remove operations.
              - O(n) Add function for duplicate data.
- NewIndexed(vals ...cmp.Ordered)  : Returns new List (with indexed searching) with vals [constrained by type in cmp.Ordered] added.
        NOTE: - Double the Memory footprint.
              - O(1) Find operations.
              - O(1) Remove Operations.
              - O(1) Add function called for duplicate.
- l.Add(vals ...cmp.Order)         : Adds vals to List.
- l.Find(v t)                      : Returns Node from List which has Val v (or nil).
- l.Last()                         : Returns last Node from List (or nil).
- l.Remove(vals ...cmp.Order)      : Removes vals from List.
- l.Size()                         : Returns size of the List.
- l.Start()                        : Returns first Node from the List (or nil).
- l.Values()                       : Returns sorted slice of List's Values (for compatibility and ease of use).



